{"title":"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">2013 AMC 12A #19</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems\">2013 AMC 10A #23</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Number_Theoretic_Power_of_a_Point)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Number Theoretic Power of a Point)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Similar_to_#1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Similar to #1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aac3ee19b22616068ded3a68e1204ab73ef7f670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9c1024e5e87080b0b7321c60bfd8a823047430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=97$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.  A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  Moreover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40e341674d6c973ae0dd53dace5036995f31997b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BX}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5895bfa441a2027d808cec50fa4da5229e07e89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CX}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> have integer lengths.  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/186d17c8f4b240117d6f37948a508b751d49dddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 11\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 28\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 33\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 61\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Number_Theoretic_Power_of_a_Point.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Number_Theoretic_Power_of_a_Point)\">Solution 1 (Number Theoretic Power of a Point)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Number Theoretic Power of a Point)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd0d1ded44edd12c5c2ea6290b65bde3a31d2eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d57a7d3459de8353ddcb527dc4c2038902d3154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> meets the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7370a7b3a820622f89dcd80da5b19d135ce9175c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AZ = AY = 86$\" width=\"121\" height=\"13\" />.  Using the Power of a Point (Secant-Secant Power Theorem), we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e965f83c17df6775254b47a7fb16342741bc11bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(p+q) = (97-86)(97+86)= 11(183) = 11 * 3 * 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"423\" height=\"20\" />.  We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65cfdc5838fc3c6d839488e35ee13f03dc88c381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q&gt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.  We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d44e74bedc35135ff49606762920ff5ab5b13ee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> by the Triangle Inequality on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af253e8b1b795df12f128aad8ff98d491a56fad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> so we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5e142c28844cf10740ca4a7d9715b407c83deff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = p+q = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"183\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Minor edits by Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Similar_to_.231.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Similar_to_#1)\">Solution 2 (Similar to #1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Similar to #1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35d6e54265614e29c8ef0ba0958dbd4184aa656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX=x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d496c593169667460f842f180883f4bb6239659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX=y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> Let the circle intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and the diameter including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect the circle again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710fb5fa3adedd7a16739e543d846747adbe05b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\nUse power of a point on point C to the circle centered at A.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b6b05be605fdab9f3a566cff05e3da59d02f86f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX \\cdot CB=CD \\cdot CE \\Rightarrow x(x+y)=(97-86)(97+86) \\Rightarrow x(x+y)=3*11*61.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"640\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6a8f32c0a71fdf2dff1cac3ce16c24effc4637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y&gt;x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> so we have three solution pairs for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/0496462fa495efacdc75e37b6b58b4cfb995ee93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,x+y)=(1,2013),(3,671),(11,183),(33,61).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"383\" height=\"20\" />\nBy the Triangle Inequality, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5fa012b23489923edc140692ee0db390b6760d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> yields a possible length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b38ea2ad11700e9ce9e76c2ad7a237a9e0e1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX+CX=BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9f7e2dbd37a9a79efc2d8c180c0fa57defe6b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }61}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"72\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Minor edits by Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/4413f31f90b322835d31bb200de469091dded18b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2); import olympiad; import graph;  pair A,B,C,D,E; A = (0,0); B = (70,51); C = (97,0); D = (82,29); E = (76,40);  draw(Circle((0,0),86.609)); draw(A--B--C--A); draw(A--B--E--A); draw(A--D); dot(A); dot(B,blue); dot(C); dot(D,blue); dot(E); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;E&quot;,E,NE); label(&quot;86&quot;,(A+B)/2,NW); label(&quot;86&quot;,(A+D)/2,SE); label(&quot;97&quot;,(A+C)/2,S); label(&quot;h&quot;,(A+E)/2,N); label(&quot;k&quot;,(E+D)/2,NE); label(&quot;k&quot;,(B+E)/2,NE); label(&quot;m&quot;,(C+D)/2,NE);   fill(anglemark(A,E,D,100),black); label(&quot;$90^\\circ$&quot;,anglemark(A,E,D),3*S); [/asy]\" width=\"625\" height=\"578\" />\n</p><p>We first draw the height of isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and get two equations by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>.\nFirst, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929cf339406f576a4959214bc60b44e23ede3471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 + k^2 = 86^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />. Second, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/954f1e9c0f215186415fe06021c43ec88ff6b06f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 + (k + m)^2 = 97^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />.\nSubtracting these two equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c85adc465464c24cfbed62ae9d3bedc86b2472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2km + m^2 = 97^2 - 86^2 = (97 - 86)(97 + 86) = 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"408\" height=\"19\" />.\nWe then add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> to both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/233a6cad703853cf497f0221e93d054ad43404cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + 2km + m^2 = 2013 + k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" />.\nWe then complete the square to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bccc8615c8bcc660177861944d2bb4a59e931b60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k + m)^2 = 2013 + k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"19\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> are both integers, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4fbf460ed8d30da9d7cc5f9c6ac77ca0e64547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013 + k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> is a square number. Simple guess and check reveals that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65aaeaa631df0effaafea93a9d3f7197d9672677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eac2a1fc37211987d12dd6a0081bba8a6d041c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 33$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c0890d4aa1142c1f39931a7109c9c8470843d5f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC} = 2k + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />, so we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff0bdd5d8d55a71140e9db00eef80e03518286c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC} = \\boxed{(D)~61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b91ba806b1b32202ba906ee5e144c46c884920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phantom{solution and diagram by bobjoe123}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"262\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baaf047f3064e842eee50196f41003a1a0174ab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX.$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82e88b3efdcfe5340faa5a70a547e07bbaf9d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABX$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4a588d1cae136c1316f1ced8d840269d7bd24d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=AB=86,EB=EX,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a366cbdcabf8f0f92a22d30d3b1c075a028a2c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC+EB=EC+EX.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa486ff7d6445cedcfe8570f22a269c48079e773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(EC+EX)(EC-EX)=EC^2-EX^2=(97^2-AE^2)-(86^2-AE^2)=97^2-86^2=2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"712\" height=\"19\" /> by the Pythagorean Theorem. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e174ac585a9db3bb309aeb07373d3e52cba3a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC+EX=\\boxed{(D)~61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"171\" height=\"29\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b36bbec3504f3ba15a25e71b144d7865864b9820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$97&gt;EC+EX&gt;EC-EX=\\frac{2013}{EC+EX}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"344\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>~dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can apply Stewarts to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> with cevian <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91669293c3747bdff89982422cbbd7e40a8f781f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3dbb031231f10cdc8e6ccad7217ee116509dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = b$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565fb57aed1d00a7f499cae95a5605e201cf4917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX = c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> We can write the equation,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab51745eba0dfeea39c090c86c4c2caaa3aeca7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[bc(b+c) + 86^2(b+c) = 97^2(b) + 86^2(c).\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"20\" />\nNow we do a clever set of changes to factor,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d77eaa39221128641c219b2122d8ed5fc408c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[bc(b+c) = 97^2(b) + 86^2(c) - 86^2(b+c) = 97^2(b)+86^2(c-(b+c)).\\]\" width=\"528\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c34c3f41031a500bc158e765867bb134d26ece.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[bc(b+c)=97^2(b)+86^2(-b) = b(97^2-86^2).\\]\" width=\"346\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f778c853cff2487f75ecbae9e467e183462d0e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c(b+c) = 97^2 - 86^2 = 11\\cdot 183 = 3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 61.\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"20\" />\nNow we can just use the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f50da79af283c409eb8462481a1ff7ebe85c678b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> to find what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is and an allowed value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64e47835ac272c805cf8d4b51cb6b4c4ec2d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> Using triangle inequality we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/9212ab8b5531907eece52b6a58026a5aa774b58a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[11 &lt; BC = b+c &lt; 183.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"14\" /> Therefore applying these restrictions the only value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9bbeb7caa1770d1d3cb842655f27e245b08188f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abdad103a89e8105327ac90f405444a09f282f1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" /> with corresponding values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effcf85fc3473f3b3116c56ed705d561c7585aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5b21748045f7c2557e6103a7b5c687aac51bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 28.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Mathkiddus\" title=\"User:Mathkiddus\">mathkiddus</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 6 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155848f5bfb766fb49205ff77fe26f25d8e7e5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = BC$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc63a47aebafda96cb47b67d5a84202f18a3674a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = XC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/16489065f4795f88c29496e4eb71452d049683e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle BCA = \\angle XCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"172\" height=\"14\" />. Using law of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/1531c537f6ffd4711e2e66914d5ff50558ca753d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AXC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dee926d4d0eee457999ea7874c30d7eca3c121.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{97^2-86^2 + x^2}{2\\cdot97x} = \\frac{97^2-86^2 + y^2}{2\\cdot97y}\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a197f99262e4a181378cfd9f2ce59c0311c0dbf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2013 + x^2)y = (2013 + y^2)x\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31d46ebd755a34b4a51d179c65e2c781cbb047dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2013(x-y) = xy(x-y)\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/2704d5f94cff13ca7d63ac988c2e277034d2bc40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y = \\overline{BX}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"21\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> is nonzero, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a782ecb564718f8457aadbcdc982d8958a330c7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy = 2013\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />\nNow you can list factors of 2013 and use the triangle innequlity as above solutions to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997b9d8aba6ec1fc5259c66fcaac3529921d170b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{(D)~61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f1nxu8MWWKc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f1nxu8MWWKc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=2692\">https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=2692</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A\">2013 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"201